# The judgement in the hall (story "The Nightglass Charge"): Kael kneels bound before Mayor Edrin
# Vale; the accuser and the bought guard press the charge, the defence takes the evidence apart,
# the witnesses are heard, and the mayor judges. Each beat is one side's move; whoever the line
# is put to answers it (the addressee judge), the mayor when it is put to the hall. The verdict
# is played, not scripted: the last beat asks the mayor for his judgement and he gives the one
# the hearing has earned. Needs `hall-photo-fresh.png` (the photographic hall) behind the scene
# (scanned, named, every character with a persona) after `arrest.beats` and `arrest-march.beats`;
# everyone starts clean (below).
# speaker | what the speaker sets out to do (their goal; they word it themselves)
@keeper town_mayor
@keeper_situation Presiding from your raised chair in the town hall, the hall full of townsfolk, over the judgement of a sword for hire who kneels bound on the floor before you, charged with stealing the Nightglass dagger from the bladesmith's stall and cutting the watchman who tried to stop him.
@speaker_situation In the town hall before the mayor on his raised chair, the hall full of townsfolk, at the judgement of a sword for hire who kneels bound on the floor, charged with stealing the Nightglass dagger from the bladesmith's stall and cutting the watchman who tried to stop him.
@frames frames=arrest-judgement-b
@frames hold=30
@frames max_frames=10
@frames parallel=2
@frames scene=A plain timber-and-plaster town hall with whitewashed walls, heavy beams, small leaded windows and flat grey daylight, townsfolk standing behind; on a raised wooden chair at the left the grey-haired mayor in a dark robe and a heavy chain; in front of him the heavy merchant in a dark coat with a fur collar holds up a dagger; the dark-haired woman sergeant in a steel cap and leather holds a sealed warrant; in the centre the blond bearded man in a fur mantle kneels bound with rope on the cobbles, the broad dark-bearded guard in mail and a steel cap gripping his shoulder; at a wooden rail to the right stand the four companions (a dark-bearded man, a young brown-haired woman, a red-bearded man, a dark-haired woman) and the grey-bearded bladesmith in a leather apron; at the bottom right a sturdy fruit seller woman in a headscarf sits with a basket of apples.
# Everyone starts clean: what each remembers of earlier runs is reset (run 70: Kael "remembered"
# run 69's acquittal mid-hearing), then each knows the names they learned by the end of the march.
